# Smoke: setup on an empty project through the first accepted write, the Profile.
id: setup-smoke
skill: highway-setup
through: highway-profile
fixture: empty
smoke: yes
open: /highway-setup
ask: What would you like to call your Highway repository?
say: northwind-highway
ask-pattern: Do you already have something I can use
say: [edit] Northwind Outfitters (https://northwind.example) is an online retailer of outdoor clothing and camping gear run by a team of twelve. We want to ship every order within one business day and grow repeat customers by a fifth this year. We plan to automate routine warehouse work and keep a small, managed stack. We protect customer data before adding features and prefer services we already run.
ask: What would you add, correct, or remove?
say: [accept] Looks good.
ask-pattern: \?
say: [decline] Let's stop setup here for now.
writes: library/**
writes: requests/requests.md
writes: discoveries/discoveries.md
writes: adrs/adrs.md
writes: architectures/architectures.md
writes: implementations/implementations.md
writes: implementations/capabilities.md
writes: code/code.md
writes: code/integrations.md
expect: template library/knowledge/profile.md :: profile-record.md
expect: template requests/requests.md :: request-catalog.md
expect: template discoveries/discoveries.md :: discovery-catalog.md
expect: template adrs/adrs.md :: adr-catalog.md
expect: template architectures/architectures.md :: architecture-catalog.md
expect: template implementations/implementations.md :: implementation-catalog.md
expect: template implementations/capabilities.md :: capability-catalog.md
expect: template code/code.md :: codify-catalog.md
expect: template code/integrations.md :: codify-integrations.md
expect: template library/coding-standards/codify-platforms.md :: codify-platforms.md
expect: template library/coding-standards/coding-standards.md :: coding-standards-catalog.md
expect: template library/knowledge/assessment-findings.md :: assessment-findings.md
expect: template library/knowledge/storage.md :: storage.md
